  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m02-s001",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 7060,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all for joining. Today is about sequencing the route optimizer migration and agreeing the first milestones."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s002",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-b",
      "startMs": 7310,
      "endMs": 15130,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Before we start, for anyone new, I'm Marcus Webb, CIO at Halden Freight. Sarah and Ravi are with me."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s003",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-c",
      "startMs": 15380,
      "endMs": 20920,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Sarah Okonkwo, I lead procurement here, so contracts and licensing come through me."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s004",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-d",
      "startMs": 21170,
      "endMs": 29750,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Ravi Menon, integration lead. I've been at Halden since 2019, so I know where most of the old integrations are buried."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s005",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 30000,
      "endMs": 34400,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And JJ from our side will lead the migration engineering."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s006",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-e",
      "startMs": 34650,
      "endMs": 39810,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Hi all. I've read through the architecture pack, it's a good start."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s007",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 40060,
      "endMs": 45220,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So the first question is sequencing. Carrier data or driver schedules first?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s008",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-d",
      "startMs": 45470,
      "endMs": 52530,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Carrier data. It's smaller, it changes slowly, and if we get it wrong nobody misses a shift."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s009",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-b",
      "startMs": 52780,
      "endMs": 59840,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I agree. Driver schedules touch payroll, I don't want those moving until we trust the new system."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s010",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 60090,
      "endMs": 66010,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then we migrate carrier data first and driver schedules after. Everyone comfortable with that?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s011",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-c",
      "startMs": 66260,
      "endMs": 71420,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes, that also lines up with the licensing, which I'll come to."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s012",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-e",
      "startMs": 71670,
      "endMs": 77590,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Works for me. It also lets us test the pipelines on something low risk."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s013",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 77840,
      "endMs": 79200,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Sarah, licensing?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s014",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-c",
      "startMs": 79450,
      "endMs": 89170,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The current optimizer license expires at the end of April. We cannot let it lapse before we've cut over, so that's our hard deadline."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s015",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-b",
      "startMs": 89420,
      "endMs": 95340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "End of April is non-negotiable from my side too, the renewal quote was absurd."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s016",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 95590,
      "endMs": 99230,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Understood. JJ, what's realistic for a dry run?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s017",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-e",
      "startMs": 99480,
      "endMs": 105780,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I can have the migration scripts ready for a full dry run in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s018",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 106030,
      "endMs": 110050,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good. Ravi, what do you need to give JJ?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s019",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-d",
      "startMs": 110300,
      "endMs": 116980,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "He needs the historical routes. I'll export the last two years of historical routes by Friday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s020",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-e",
      "startMs": 117230,
      "endMs": 122770,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Two years is plenty. Can you include the depot codes in the export?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s021",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-d",
      "startMs": 123020,
      "endMs": 125140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes, depot codes included."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s022",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 125390,
      "endMs": 129030,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What about support during the cutover weekend itself?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s023",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-b",
      "startMs": 129280,
      "endMs": 135580,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Whoever's on call that weekend can watch the cutover, we don't need a special rota."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s024",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 135830,
      "endMs": 142130,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'd still like a named contact, but we can settle that closer to the date."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s025",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-b",
      "startMs": 142380,
      "endMs": 152860,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Fair. One more thing, I'm mostly working out of the Rotterdam office these days, so if we need to meet in person that's where I'll be."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s026",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 153110,
      "endMs": 155610,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Noted, thanks Marcus. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s027",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-c",
      "startMs": 155860,
      "endMs": 162160,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Just that any new vendor terms need to come to me before anyone signs anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02-s028",
      "speakerId": "m02-spk-a",
      "startMs": 162410,
      "endMs": 170990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Absolutely. So: carrier data first, dry run in three weeks, historical routes by Friday, and the April license deadline. Thanks everyone."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Halden route optimizer migration planning\n\n**Date:** January 15\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), JJ (Larkspur Labs), Marcus Webb (Halden Freight), Sarah Okonkwo (Halden Freight), Ravi Menon (Halden Freight)\n\n## Summary\n\nPlanning session for migrating Halden Freight off its legacy route optimizer. Marcus Webb (CIO) sponsors the work; Sarah Okonkwo leads procurement and owns licensing; Ravi Menon is the integration lead and has been at Halden since 2019. JJ leads migration engineering for Larkspur.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Carrier data migrates first**, driver schedules afterwards. Carrier data is smaller and slower-changing, and driver schedules touch payroll, so they wait until the new system is trusted.\n\n## Key facts\n\n- The current optimizer license expires at the end of April. Sarah and Marcus both treat this as a hard deadline; the renewal quote was described as absurd.\n- Any new vendor terms must go through Sarah before anyone signs.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **JJ** — have the migration scripts ready for a full dry run in three weeks.\n- **Ravi Menon** — export the last two years of historical routes, including depot codes, by Friday.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- Cutover weekend support: Marcus suggested that whoever's on call that weekend can watch the cutover. Alex would still like a named contact; to be settled closer to the date.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Marcus mostly works out of the Rotterdam office now, so in-person meetings would be there.\n"
  },
